WEBVTT

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:29.820
Just give me that country.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.220
I'd rather stay.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:46.310
He can't have you, but give me Park Avenue.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.000
The chores.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.580
Fresh.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.120
Fresh air.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.240
You are my wife.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.190
I was so excited I didn't even see you.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:24.440
There's a story about you opening your law office

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.500
right here on the front page of the World Guardian.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:28.150
Listen to this.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:29.840
Oliver Wendell Douglas

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:38.640
announces that continued on page two he is opening law offices with continued on page three

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.000
brian williams a local boy who continued on page one

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:50.560
page one graduated with high honors from continued on page four

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:59.970
the state school of continued next week real cliffhanger ain't it of all this

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.010
What time do we have to go to the office?

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.760
What are you wearing?

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:09.580
It's my secretary outfit.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.180
Are you going to be their secretary?

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.990
Not if you wear that.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:21.980
I wanted to ask you, who is this Brian Williams?

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:25.820
I mentioned on pages 1, 2, 3, 1 and 4.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.840
You don't know him? He grew up here in Hooterville.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:29.980
Is he?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.030
a tall boy with green hair. Green hair? No, that was Betty Abernathy. She used to eat chlorophyll

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:44.260
and it went to her head. Oh, you. Look, I got a list of things I want you to do around here today

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:49.740
while I'm at the office. Now, first, I want you to spray the tomatoes. Oliver, how's this? Oh,

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:55.100
well, that's better. Yeah, I've always liked you in that. You mean you've seen me buy this before?

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.440
Several times. I see what else I can find.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.160
Hey, I've never tell a woman you've seen her wear the same dress before.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.060
I always tell my girl she's wearing the same dress.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.240
I've been telling her that for three years now.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:13.920
But let's get back to the things I want you to do.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.480
Now, after you spray the tomatoes, I want you to weed the 40 acres of corn.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.140
And when you're done with that, that'll be a week from next Tuesday.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.420
Yeah, I'm counting on you to keep the farm running for me.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:24.970
I'll do my best.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:29.820
I'll get up early in the morning and milk the cow, feed the chicken, slot the hogs, make the beds.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.690
Tote that barge, lift that veil.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.490
Old man Douglas got drunk and landed in jail.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:38.990
Have you ever seen this one before?

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:40.160
Not on you.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:44.140
But that's the one my girlfriend's been wearing for the last three years.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.760
It's fine. No, no, come on, let's go.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:47.700
Just a second.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:51.970
I bought a present for you to help you launch your new office.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:54.520
A bottle of champagne?

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.840
Yes, ma'am, and it's almost half full.

00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:59.870
How do you buy a half a bottle of champagne?

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:03.540
You just have to know some other guy that wants to buy a half a bottle of champagne.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:08.890
Listen, if it's a little flat, you can just put some salt in it and it'll foam up.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.430
Put it back on the ice and we'll foam it up when we get home.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.850
Thank you. Now, come on, Lisa, let's go.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:16.510
Goodbye and good luck.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:18.020
And don't worry about a thing.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:21.980
Oliver Mandel Douglas.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.450
